# Domain Rules

## Domains

| Domain | Path | Responsibility |
|--------|------|----------------|
| booking | `features/booking/` | Reservation request orchestration |
| capacity | `features/capacity/` | Passenger/luggage eligibility and recommendations |
| pricing | `features/pricing/` | Price calculation and quotes |
| locations | `features/locations/` | Regions, airports, hotels, transfer points |
| vehicles | `features/vehicles/` | Vehicle categories and capacity |
| extras | `features/extras/` | Optional add-on services |
| customers | `features/customers/` | Customer contact management |
| admin | `features/admin/` | Admin operations (future) |

## Module structure

Each domain follows:
```
features/<domain>/
  components/
  domain/      # pure logic — no DB, React, or server imports
  schemas/     # Zod validation schemas
  server/
    service.ts     # orchestration
    repository.ts  # persistence
  types/
  utils/
```

## Allowed

- Pure functions in `features/<domain>/domain/`
- Domain services orchestrating repositories
- Zod schemas colocated with domain
- Snapshot pattern for historical data
- Enum constants from `src/db/schema/enums.ts`

## Forbidden

- Cross-domain direct repository access (go through service)
- Undocumented business rules
- Hard-coded status strings
- Capacity logic inside pricing service
- Hardcoded luggage vehicle prices or codes

## Before modifying a domain

Read `/docs/DOMAIN_MODEL.md`, `/docs/BOOKING_ENGINE.md`, `/docs/PRICE_ENGINE.md` as applicable.

## After changing domain rules

Update the relevant `/docs/*.md` file. No undocumented behavior.
